   "title": "Read me",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "MESH -> TURNTABLE, for looking at\n\nRenders 8 flat unlit frames.  Good enough to check a silhouette; for\nform, use scripts/render_sheet.py, which lights it and puts a grey\nclay on anything untextured.\n\nmesh_file_path is a CONTAINER path: /app/output/mesh/<name>.glb\n\n---\n\nSaved mesh -> 8 facings on the ISOMETRIC diagonal. For a 2:1\ndimetric grid (tile 64 wide by 32 high) the camera is at 30\ndegrees elevation and looks down the diagonal between the world\naxes: a unit facing north/east/south/west must be rendered at\n45/135/225/315, NOT 0/90/180/270, or the sprite faces square-on\nwhile the ground runs diagonally beneath it. Azimuth is clamped\nto [-180,180], so eight facings are -135..180 step 45. Load 3D\nMesh takes a STRING CONTAINER path. Masks are MASK and need\nMaskToImage before SaveImage."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
